Language English
Debug Off

Book Hall1 Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page PlaceHall1
		Triggered By @ExploreHall1ViaDiningRoom
		
		Prolog """
			The door has a dirty push plate. When you push on it, you discover
			it's locked. An investigator with the {c:QItemBrassKey} can open
			this door.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Text """
			When you open the door, the rush of cold, stale air sends a chill
			down your spine.

			You stop for a moment and look back down at the footsteps leading
			to this door. You wonder how the air feels so stale if this door
			has been opened recently.
		"""
	
		$mythosHall = true
		exploredHall1 = true
	End Page PlaceHall1

	
	Page PlaceJournal
		Not Visible When foundJournal
		
		Text QItemJournal """
			While you are looking at the prints, the book on the floor gets
			your attention, so you reach over to pick it up. Gain the
			{c:QItemJournal} unique item.
			
			You look at the book you picked up:  small, thin, and
			leather-bound. You flip through the pages: 	it's a journal.
			The first entry was scrawled last Sunday.

			Maybe you should hold onto it to give back to Benjamin when you
			see him later today. And maybe take a quick look yourself.

			Discard this Search token.
			
			An investigator holding the {c:QItemJournal} Unique Item can
			interact with it in the app.
		"""
		
		foundJournal = true
		foundJournalInDiningRoom = true
	End Page PlaceJournal

	Page PlaceHall1Tile
		Add TileHall1, TokenDoorHall1!, TokenWallHall1!
		Remove TokenExploreHall1ViaDiningRoom
		
		Text """
			You look through the doorway to find a hall. It is clear that it
			was intended for the servants:  plain and dark. Place the
			{c:TileHall1} tile, a door, and a wall as indicated.
			
			Move one space space into the explored area.
		"""
	End Page PlaceHall1Tile
	
	Page PlaceExploreGallery
		Add TokenExploreGalleryViaHall1!

		Text """
			There is a door to your immediate right. Place an Explore token as
			indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceExploreGallery
	
	Page PlaceHall1Evidence
		Add TokenSearchHall1Rug!

		Text """
			You look down. The rug on the floor is old and beautiful, if
			dirty and poorly cared for. One corner is folded up and looks
			like it has been that way for years. You should probably put
			it back so you don't trip over it.
			
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		If Not foundJournalInDiningRoom Then Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page PlaceHall1Evidence
	
	Page SearchRug
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchHall1Rug
	
		Prolog "The corner of the rug is folded over."
		Button "Search"
		
		Text QItemEvidenceHall1 """
			You lean down to straighten the rug. You play with it for a bit,
			but have trouble getting it to stay flat--the fold has been there
			too long. You lift the rug a little try again. There's a piece of
			paper under the rug. You pick it up; it has a diagram of a tabletop
			with arcane symbols. Maybe it's part of some ritual? You've heard
			the people in this town have some funny beliefs.

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceHall1} Unique Item and
			1 {clue}, then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchHall1Rug
		foundEvidenceCount = foundEvidenceCount + 1
		Exit
	End Page SearchRug
	
	Page SearchPainting
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchHall1Painting
		
		Prolog "The painting glows with unnatural light."
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			The painting is of a girl. The work is
			stunning and the girl looks so lifelike, it's as if she could just
			step through the frame. She's wearing a white dress and looks
			serious.

			When you blink, you think the painting has moved but you know that
			can't happen. You also notice that there is no dust anywhere on
			the painting or its frame. You feel like there's something else
			you've missed, but you dismiss it and turn away. Gain 1 {clue},
			then discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchHall1Painting

		Goto SearchPainting2
	End Page SearchPainting

	Page SearchPainting2
		Not Visible

		Add TokenSarah!
		
		Text """
			As you turn around, you notice two shadows on the wall:  yours
			and... you quickly look back at the painting. The girl is not
			there. Startled, you turn to run back; move 1 space toward the
			{c:TileDiningRoom}. You are brought up short when the girl from the
			painting is standing in front of you.

			Place the Green Girl token as indicated. Shocked, you take 1 Horror
			({will} negates).
		"""
		
		foundSarahsPainting = true
		Exit
	End Page SearchPainting2
	
	Page TalkToSarah
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @TalkToSarah
		
		Prolog """
			She is a pretty girl in the the first blush of youth--maybe 11 or
			12 years old. She has curly hair with emerald green ribbons and a
			bright white dress that stands out in the dingy hallway.

			She looks at you like she wants to say
			something, but is holding back. She still looks serious, but also
			concerned and maybe afraid. You think your mind is playing
			tricks on you because she seems to be glowing. And a 
			little bit transparent.

			She will only speak with {c:EventChosenInvestigator}.		
		"""
		Button "Talk to her"
		
		Text """
			She brightens up, both emotionally and in her glow. <<It's good to
			see you again. I thought you had forgotten me after that night.
			I've missed you.>>

			You are surprised at what she says. <i>Who is this girl? Why does
			she think she knows me?</i>

			<<I know you have many
			questions,>> she starts, <<and I'll answer all of them. But first,
			you need to know that you and your friends are in danger. We must
			move quickly.>>

			Move the Green Girl token to your investigator card.
			She will follow you to whatever ends you meet in this house. While
			she is with you, you gain +1 {will}.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSarah
		foundSarah = true
		Exit
	End Page TalkToSarah
	
End Book Hall1